{"seq":3,"slug":"metabolism-energy","title":"代谢与能量系统","docCount":3,"url":"/h/health-medicine/nutrition-science/metabolism-energy","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"cellular-energy-metabolism","title":"细胞能量代谢","url":"/h/health-medicine/nutrition-science/metabolism-energy/cellular-energy-metabolism","wordCount":2554,"readingTime":11},{"seq":2,"slug":"metabolic-flexibility-and-adaptation","title":"代谢灵活性与适应","url":"/h/health-medicine/nutrition-science/metabolism-energy/metabolic-flexibility-and-adaptation","wordCount":2402,"readingTime":10},{"seq":3,"slug":"hormonal-regulation-of-metabolism","title":"激素对代谢的调控","url":"/h/health-medicine/nutrition-science/metabolism-energy/hormonal-regulation-of-metabolism","wordCount":2897,"readingTime":12}],"introMarkdown":"# 代谢与能量系统\n\n本章深入人体能量代谢的核心机制——从 ATP 合成的分子生物学到整体代谢灵活性（Metabolic Flexibility），再到激素网络对营养物质分配的精密调控。\n\n学习重点：\n\n- 细胞层面的三大能量代谢通路：糖酵解、三羧酸循环、氧化磷酸化\n- 代谢灵活性的概念：人体如何在糖类与脂肪氧化之间切换\n- 胰岛素、瘦素、皮质醇等激素如何协调代谢状态\n\n理解代谢系统是连接\"吃什么\"与\"身体如何利用\"的桥梁。掌握这些知识，你将能理解为何同样的饮食在不同时间、不同生理状态下会产生不同的代谢结果。\n"}